ey":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:06:50-08:00","id":780487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780472#post780472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heir to the throne is assassinated. To everyone, she is dead : a magnificent burial is organised, and the kingdom lives on. Soon, the vizier uses the void to proclaim himself heir, as he planned to do all along. But the heir survived : she is in the palace, every day, trying to get people to react to her. Every single person who would be able to recognise her forgets that she is alive as soon as they take their eyes off her. Every minute is a struggle, as not matter how long she spends explaining what is happening to her family, servants or rivals, they forget all about it as soon as they leave the room.<br /> <br /> A man wakes up in the body of his mule. He is beaten, and forced to work in his own farm. The one who took his place is simple of mind, loves to torment him, and seems to love carrots.<br /> <br /> After a drinking binge, a man comes home, to find another version of him living in his house. The other him never went drinking.<br /> <br /> Etc... etc..</div> </div> </div> </div>When certain powers intervene in this sort of thing, a Getimian is created, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:34:30-08:00","id":780497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780487#post780487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When certain powers intervene in this sort of thing, a Getimian is created, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's possible too, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:42:03-08:00","id":780502,"title":"","content":"Trying to sum up how I'd think of random Fate glitches, I guess I'd: <br /> <br /> a) Just make something exist which shouldn't exist - Why is this city here? History says it ceased to exist 200 years ago. What effect does this have on the region? How do you smooth this over, by travelling around and persuading the &quot;citizens&quot; of the city that they've actually had lives elsewhere, and creating a campaign of information that the city never existed, and then faking up the city as more aged and weathered than it actually is, etc.<br /> <br /> b) Give something the properties of something else (including a destiny) that it oughtn't have - following a surge in the Wyld and certain bizarre occult convergences, the Linowans have suddenly assumed part of the destiny of the local birds, and so use the power of flight to make ceaseless warfare on the Haltan. Someone oughta fix that, as it's obviously not what we want to happen.<br /> <br /> c) Something has happened which ought to happen but in the wrong order (the historical cart has come before the horse), and you have to flex wildly to put it in the right order<br /> <br /> (Wasn't there a random generator for these someone built, or am I misremembering?)<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty here for me with these has always been how these weave as part of a compelling larger plot, driven by heroic passions and other such things of heroic wuxia epics, rather than being random world-goes-derp that the Sidereal character has to fix.<br /> <br /> You can make a lot of how demons and fae and undead exploit the opportunities created by fate glitches (that city that wasn't supposed to be there is a fine place for demons to cross over into the world of Creation, etc)... but the Sidereals aren't really the Watchers or Libra of Kekkai Sensen (secret organisations whose mission is to fight and manage demons), so there's a limit to that.<br /> <br /> In the fictional antecedents of the Sidereals, The Traveller in Black fixes glitches which are really the suffusion of ancient primal magic into the world, driven by foolish mortals seeking easy power and mischief by petty chaotic godlings - but it is kind of a loosely held together collection of short stories, so a bad example of how these can hang together into a great narrative (and the Traveller is more of forger of natural law in the world and banisher of the Wyld, something Sidereals seem less set up to be in Exalted, for whatever reason). While the Otherhood of the Great Work of Time don't really fix glitches so much as adjust history towards what they think it ought to be.<br /> <br /> Not that fixing Fate glitches could be fun (because dream up a pretty crazy situation, and then have players apply their characters skills to it fixing it should be), I guess I'm saying it seems too reactive and status quo oriented and random to really make too much of as substance beyond challenge of the week parts of the character's Sidereal career which building up to the *real* arcs of the story, and to establish the sort of person they are before introducing your Sidereal characters' *real* proactive plans to change the world and the real interpersonal dramas and rivalries and Celestial politics that actually motivate them (like a substory that introduces a boss or rival or lover who can become more important in the story than they appear to be at first).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:01:34-08:00","id":780509,"title":"","content":"The mini-series The Lost Room is good for this.<br /> For those who've never heard of it the premise is similar to Warehouse 13 but it's a cosmic horror story involving a motel room that was erased from history in 1961 but still sort of exists and the items in the room imbued with strange properties that vary from useful to just bizarre.<br /> <br /> For example the watch boils an egg if you place it on the face, but just an egg but if you combine it with the knife it grants telepathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:30:23-08:00","id":780517,"title":"","content":"Also this :<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tBJe53IA9DE\" data-code=\"tBJe53IA9DE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tBJe53IA9DE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:34:11-08:00","id":780520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780509#post780509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mini-series The Lost Room is good for this.<br /> For those who've never heard of it the premise is similar to Warehouse 13 but it's a cosmic horror story involving a motel room that was erased from history in 1961 but still sort of exists and the items in the room imbued with strange properties that vary from useful to just bizarre.<br /> <br /> For example the watch boils an egg if you place it on the face, but just an egg but if you combine it with the knife it grants telepathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, the Lost Room is all kinds of awesome. and utterly worth watching as reference for any weird game, awesome WoD/Mage the Awakening fodder too (personally, i always suspected WoD: Reliquary was inspired by the mini-series).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, wasn't there a bit on this in a table on 1e sidereals?<br /> <br /> I think they had a table with an arrangement of possible missions and collaterals of glitches, with some potentially snowballing from minor to greater into epic, while doing all kind of stuff from weirdness comparable to minor thaumaturgic rituals to terrestrial or celestial circle sorcery equivalent level bugs and potential demonic/fae/underworld intrusion to boot. Might be entertaining to adapt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:26:13-08:00","id":780655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780520#post780520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, wasn't there a bit on this in a table on 1e sidereals?<br /> <br /> I think they had a table with an arrangement of possible missions and collaterals of glitches, with some potentially snowballing from minor to greater into epic, while doing all kind of stuff from weirdness comparable to minor thaumaturgic rituals to terrestrial or celestial circle sorcery equivalent level bugs and potential demonic/fae/underworld intrusion to boot. Might be entertaining to adapt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that table exists than I'm sad. With all the 1e copypasta in 2e Sidereals they couldn't port the best part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:25:26-08:00","id":780802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780655#post780655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that table exists than I'm sad. With all the 1e copypasta in 2e Sidereals they couldn't port the best part.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bunch of tables actually, going from kinds of missions, straightforward or opposed, the kind of forces that might interfere with the PCs' action in the later case, the tables about fate snarling collaterals - and one to determine how much time the PCs might have to either do a mission or troubleshoot a fate glitch before that consolidates itself or evolves into something else. Fun stuff with good mix-up or replay potential i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:26:11-08:00","id":780804,"title":"","content":"The same cat walks past you twice... and then weird people want you to take drugs being all mystical about it,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T21:47:13-08:00","id":780910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=780472#post780472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heir to the throne is assassinated. To everyone, she is dead : a magnificent burial is organised, and the kingdom lives on. Soon, the vizier uses the void to proclaim himself heir, as he planned to do all along. But the heir survived : she is in the palace, every day, trying to get people to react to her. Every single person who would be able to recognise her forgets that she is alive as soon as they take their eyes off her. Every minute is a struggle, as not matter how long she spends explaining what is happening to her family, servants or rivals, they forget all about it as soon as they leave the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone has been reading Terry Pratchett !<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T01:38:05-08:00","id":781012,"title":"","content":"Otherwise perfectly mundane spiders start weaving messages into their webs that foretell the planned fates of the locals in several villages. This breach of security is ostensibly a minor one, but knowing one's fate with such ease can sometimes put a snarl in the most delicate threads of destiny. Farmer Jeng might learn that he will be attacked by bandits the next time he goes into town. By delaying his trip, the bandits move on a day early and end up pillaging another homestead a week early, killing the wrong people. Currently the consequences are very minor, but solving the problem is more difficult than killing all of the spiders in the area and your superiors are being pressured by Gods getting kickbacks from local divinities to fix the problem now before it gets to be a bigger problem and the area gains a great deal more official scrutiny than they are prepared to deal with..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:48:37-08:00","id":782297,"title":"","content":"As I've said elsewhere, I can see new Thaumaturgy having an interesting relationship with the Sidereals.<br /> Like maybe there's a version of the tea leaf ritual that actually dooms the people whose futures are read by it or rituals with useful effects that have long term consequences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:54:02-08:00","id":782301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=782297#post782297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said elsewhere, I can see new Thaumaturgy having an interesting relationship with the Sidereals.<br /> Like maybe there's a version of the tea leaf ritual that actually dooms the people whose futures are read by it or rituals with useful effects that have long term consequences?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always wanted to make a Sidereal character that used Thaumaturgy as a cover for their real powers. <br /> <br /> &quot;How did you know that?!&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, my tea leaves told me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:57:59-08:00","id":782304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/780458-loom-and-reality-glitches-sidereal-s-everyday-life-problems?p=782297#post782297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said elsewhere, I can see new Thaumaturgy having an interesting relationship with the Sidereals.<br /> Like maybe there's a version of the tea leaf ritual that actually dooms the people whose futures are read by it or rituals with useful effects that have long term consequences?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty neat idea! I'm stealing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:59:37-08:00","id":782389,"title":"","content":"The most interesting thing about this particular part of the Sidereals job is that you can't pummel it into submission with Essence expenditure.<br /> <br /> I do not mean to imply that the other Exalt types are without depth, to forestall that accusation. Far from it! But the sort of problems their powersets are designed to deal with are, you know, comprehensible and often resolvable via direct action and application of their puissance. Even the sort of head-aching political imbroglios you can end up with in, say, a Dragon-Blooded game with a heavy<i> Game of Thrones </i>style focus on the vacant throne generally present problems where, mechanically speaking, you can just apply the appropriate amount of Essence via the appropriate Charms with a reasonable degree of success. A lot of problems Solars have are damned interesting and fun and have a lot of depth, but Solars are designed to be super crazy awesome and can usually overcome most problems by just hitting it with their Solarness until it stops being a problem.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals <i>can</i> do this as well. The parts of their job that have heavy overlap with the sort of problems other Exalt types routinely encounter (needing to solve a political dispute, someone has to die, how can I solve the mystery of the Jade Monkey by the next full moon, etc) they have their own avenues they can use to Essence them into not being problems anymore. When Iron Siaka needs to prevent a demon from slipping into Creation she can pick up her mace, beat it into a fine pink mist, and then have makeouts. When they need to make a political enemy go away they can use subtle magics to dismay their targets allies, that sort of thing. A lot of what they do is very standard...<br /> <br /> ... except when they're wearing their Fate Troubleshooter hats. How the hell do you solve a problem like &quot;there are now three Sesus Rafara's each apparently running on their own individualized destiny track&quot; or &quot;this guy dies every evening and then in the morning wakes up normally in bed. Nobody remembers him dying except himself and this one other weird guy we suspect might be the lobotomized remains of a crippled god from the time-before-time&quot; or any of the other examples extant in this thread with direct action? You<i> can't</i>.<br /> <br /> The problems are clearly solvable but they're real headaches both in-universe and at the table, which is what makes them interesting and fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}